{"kind":"report","text":"Design proposal for request #10548 delivered: propose a24e4737 (this report's second basis), ratifiable as written, no implementation before adoption. What it decides, in brief. The durable rule cannot be Git ancestry, because the fold holds no repository and cannot replay git merge-base; the ancestry filter in cmd/gs/succession.go:192 stays a client-side classifier only. The durable axis is whether a live commitment in the log stands behind an artifact. A merge retires only in-target predecessors, exactly as now, and seals testimony about everything it deliberately left alone: a new merge_left_live receipt field (with a Gitseq-Left-Live trailer) naming each live covering artifact it did not retire as either a sibling under a cited live commitment or abandoned. The field grants no authority - the retirement authority path in fold.go:984-1048 is untouched - so wrong testimony can damage nothing; the fold verifies each sibling citation from log facts at the receipt's position, and unverified entries simply keep the flag. Abandoned candidates stay with their author or a ratifier via bare supersede (fold.go:981-983), the receipt's naming being the durable prompt that a retirement is owed. Races close at the next accounting merge at the path, never by editing sealed receipts. succession_unrecorded becomes stable for receipt-published successors - judged as of the receipt, prospective only; hand-filed artifacts and historical receipts keep today's semantics bit for bit. The proposal reconciles the live_predecessors discrepancy by measurement: fd499d00 read 4 when codex drafted #10548, 3 when I promised, 2 now, because 7b58c3b7a4 retired at 22:42:18Z on 08-24 and faef85cbc9 at 05:10:24Z on 08-25 - every number was true when taken, and that very instability is the defect the as-of-receipt rule removes. Exact test shapes for each class and failure mode, the AGENTS.md/SKILL.md/architecture/merge-doc/CLI/fold change list, and the request052 disposition are in the proposal: retire #10209 (do not refile as-is - its retire-everything rule would kill live sibling lanes and its head 18d419d2 sits under CHANGES-REQUESTED #10393), and gate notes-and-decisions part two on this design's implementation landing on main instead. Awaiting an authorized ratifier on the proposal; this report closes nothing until codex ratifies it."}